WEBVTT

00:02.640 --> 00:05.660
Executive Producers: Ryuzo Shirakawa,
Akira Sato, Mitsuhisa Ishikawa

00:08.040 --> 00:11.240
Planning and Original Concept:
Production I. G

00:13.380 --> 00:16.750
Planning in Cooperation
with Mamoru Oshii (Team Oshii)

00:19.990 --> 00:23.180
Character Designer: Katsuya Terada

00:27.390 --> 00:30.730
Screenplay: Kenji Kamiyama

00:34.970 --> 00:38.200
Technical Director: Shinji Takagi

00:40.340 --> 00:41.860
Please take all your
belongings with you.

00:42.380 --> 00:45.680
This will be the last train
going to Asakusa.

00:47.710 --> 00:50.980
Animation Director: Kazuchika Kise

00:58.730 --> 01:02.020
Art Director: Yusuke Takeda

01:11.740 --> 01:15.000
Director of Visual Concept:
Hisashi Ezura

01:30.090 --> 01:33.320
Color Designer: Katsue Inoue

01:42.070 --> 01:45.270
3D CGI: Tokumitsu Kifune

01:51.950 --> 01:55.240
Filming: Miki Sakuma

02:51.170 --> 02:54.300
Post Production Supervisor:
Keiichi Momose

03:00.950 --> 03:04.350
Music: Yoshihiro Ike

03:13.230 --> 03:18.600
We will be stopping at Asakusa shortly.
This will be the final stop.

03:21.300 --> 03:24.400
Director: Hiroyuki Kitakubo

03:59.280 --> 04:01.000
Saya!

04:03.860 --> 04:05.250
Where is the chiropterate?

04:05.790 --> 04:06.440
Inside.

04:08.490 --> 04:09.670
This sword's getting dull.

04:10.580 --> 04:13.390
It's not sliding out of the sheath
as smoothly as it should.

04:14.170 --> 04:16.700
- Get me a new one.
- That's not possible.

04:17.300 --> 04:21.070
We don't have time because we just
identified another one of them.

04:21.890 --> 04:23.990
Swords of that quality
are not easy to get.

04:40.230 --> 04:41.420
What the...?

04:42.420 --> 04:44.880
This isn't a chiropterate,
did we get the wrong guy?

04:46.000 --> 04:49.320
It just hasn't changed form
yet, Louis. Now, shut up.

04:50.260 --> 04:54.410
Wait a minute. Isn't this supposed
to be within your jurisdiction?

04:55.420 --> 04:57.020
That's a regular
human corpse in there.

04:57.940 --> 05:00.040
I've already checked
the military personnel

05:00.360 --> 05:03.070
as well as
the civilian employees involved.

05:04.180 --> 05:06.940
- What do you mean?
- Hey! David!

05:06.940 --> 05:08.820
(David) They've
infiltrated the public.

05:09.140 --> 05:11.090
You want me to investigate this?

05:11.320 --> 05:13.230
Dave! Take a look inside!

05:14.330 --> 05:15.430
- Hey!
- Save it!

05:16.320 --> 05:17.520
Oh, Jesus...

05:21.680 --> 05:23.750
Wait! Saya!
Get ahold of yourself, now!

05:24.820 --> 05:25.820
Not the same thing again.

05:26.690 --> 05:29.260
Do you want to announce it
to the whole world?

05:30.020 --> 05:31.580
I can't do anything about it.

05:32.310 --> 05:33.800
You know the way it is by now.

05:34.290 --> 05:37.690
The orders from the top are
to hunt them down, no matter what.

05:38.320 --> 05:41.780
- I really don't know anything.

05:47.540 --> 05:49.660
It's all in there
and it's arranged accordingly.

05:50.550 --> 05:51.470
You can go tomorrow.

05:52.110 --> 05:55.170
I'll have your school uniform
and ID ready by then.

05:56.010 --> 05:57.830
You better read through
the file carefully.

05:58.300 --> 06:00.290
We know there's more than one...
Hey!

06:00.760 --> 06:01.980
Hey, Saya!

06:04.440 --> 06:05.270
Shit.

06:13.000 --> 06:15.170
What the hell was that all about?

06:17.640 --> 06:18.580
You asshole!

06:19.960 --> 06:20.830
What did I do?!

06:21.340 --> 06:23.110
Don't ever piss her off again!

06:23.810 --> 06:24.720
- But...
- Listen!

06:25.000 --> 06:28.800
As far as we know,
she's the only remaining original.

06:30.960 --> 06:31.710
Original?

07:16.070 --> 07:20.530
So the tap was still running
when you found her.

07:21.640 --> 07:24.970
Calm down.
You don't have to cry.

07:28.280 --> 07:33.220
I'm not too sure, but I heard Mari
was going out with an American soldier.

07:38.060 --> 07:40.890
Mari from Charade's
committed suicide.

07:40.890 --> 07:44.620
Stupid girl.
She didn't have to kill herself.

07:45.170 --> 07:48.000
Maybe she's got the "clap."

07:49.400 --> 07:51.390
You can't get upset over
a minor thing

07:51.390 --> 07:53.700
if you're doing business
with American soldiers.

07:53.700 --> 07:58.210
Did you hear about the suicide
at the base school last month?

07:58.610 --> 08:01.710
There seem to be
a lot of them lately.

08:02.780 --> 08:05.220
Apparently, everybody's really
uptight about it.

08:05.850 --> 08:09.220
How terrible.
I hope this doesn't affect business.

08:09.220 --> 08:13.880
It can't be helped if we're going
to make a living off the base.

08:14.390 --> 08:15.420
Huh?

08:15.830 --> 08:21.170
It can't be helped if we're going
to make a living off the base.

10:06.510 --> 10:10.880
Aren't you Japanese?
You are not a student here, are you?

10:12.410 --> 10:14.380
Did you pass through the office?

10:18.050 --> 10:19.780
Hey, hold on a second!

10:22.520 --> 10:24.220
Where is the principal's office?

10:24.220 --> 10:25.220
Huh?

10:29.270 --> 10:30.060
Come in.

10:31.880 --> 10:33.810
Sir, this young lady here...

10:34.110 --> 10:35.500
Ahh, Saya. You're late.

10:36.130 --> 10:37.580
I want you to say hello
to the principal.

10:41.860 --> 10:44.130
Hello. You do speak English?

10:44.450 --> 10:45.270
(David) Of course.

10:45.890 --> 10:49.190
Well then, you can go see
some classes this afternoon.

10:49.990 --> 10:54.110
But with the Halloween party coming
up we may not get much work done.

10:57.020 --> 10:58.740
Thank you very much for your help.
Goodbye.

11:08.000 --> 11:08.850
Who was that girl?

11:09.080 --> 11:10.600
She came on an introduction.

11:10.990 --> 11:13.180
She wants to join classes
for a few days.

11:15.110 --> 11:16.860
- Um, excuse me, sir...
- Huh?

11:17.290 --> 11:20.260
About the party tomorrow?

11:20.840 --> 11:21.850
Not that again.

11:22.690 --> 11:24.780
I thought we were over that by now.

11:25.520 --> 11:28.710
Yes, sir, but it isn't long
since the terrible incident.

11:29.440 --> 11:32.550
Have the students recovered
from the death of their friend?

11:32.770 --> 11:36.740
That's why we're having this party.
I've had enough of this.

11:37.650 --> 11:39.150
Now, get back to work.

11:50.370 --> 11:52.000
What the hell is this outfit?

11:52.540 --> 11:55.680
I'm not sure. It's supposed to be
a Japanese high school uniform.

11:56.480 --> 12:00.070
At any rate, another fake corpse
was found here last night,

12:00.590 --> 12:01.420
and it's the same pattern.

12:02.700 --> 12:04.000
It's happening awfully fast.

12:06.040 --> 12:07.660
I told you
there was more than one of them.

12:08.230 --> 12:11.180
We'll never find them
once they go into hibernation.

12:11.180 --> 12:13.280
We have to find them
before we get another corpse.

12:14.690 --> 12:15.930
You just listen for them.

12:17.230 --> 12:17.970
And get the sword.

12:19.640 --> 12:20.340
(David) I know.

12:50.770 --> 12:51.960
All right, that's it for today.

12:52.210 --> 12:54.400
Tomorrow we'll have
morning classes only.

12:55.790 --> 12:57.170
- I'm not through yet.

12:57.560 --> 13:00.240
Those getting things ready for
the dance meet in the assembly room,

13:01.880 --> 13:04.360
the rest of you can stay here
and get ready...

13:04.360 --> 13:06.840
Hey, are you Japanese?

13:08.600 --> 13:09.620
(Teacher) ..or old Pumpkinhead
will get you.

13:13.710 --> 13:14.670
Leave me alone.

13:16.450 --> 13:17.210
Weirdo!

13:18.460 --> 13:19.960
Come on, Linda, let's go.

15:10.340 --> 15:12.830
So, this is their "dining room" then.

15:29.700 --> 15:31.090
Oh, you scared me.

15:32.470 --> 15:34.960
What were you doing here?

15:34.960 --> 15:38.270
Nothing. I thought I had a headache.

15:38.270 --> 15:39.340
But it's gone now.

15:40.810 --> 15:42.100
Oh. Wait!

15:44.910 --> 15:46.900
Hold on a minute!

17:09.700 --> 17:12.370
Come on, the band's
going to start any minute now.

17:16.680 --> 17:18.610
- Sir?
- What is it, Sharon?

17:19.200 --> 17:21.540
Aren't you going to put on
your costumes? What's the matter?

17:22.980 --> 17:27.390
Linda told me she's not feeling very
well. It might be her anaemia again.

17:28.810 --> 17:30.610
I thought I'd go with her
to the infirmary.

17:33.830 --> 17:36.560
Again? Well, OK.
You don't need me, do you?

17:37.450 --> 17:40.470
- No, sir.
- Join us when she feels better.

17:40.790 --> 17:42.460
- You girls be careful, now.
- OK.

17:48.500 --> 17:49.470
Are you OK?

17:49.920 --> 17:51.030
It won't be too long.

18:16.270 --> 18:18.370
I'd like
to take it easy once in a while.

18:18.860 --> 18:20.510
Especially on a day like this.

18:24.920 --> 18:28.520
This isn't a very fun way
to spend Halloween, is it?

18:34.740 --> 18:37.220
Don't worry,
it's only minor anaemia.

18:38.200 --> 18:40.060
She should feel better any minute.

18:41.660 --> 18:44.020
You should really try
not to worry too much,

18:44.750 --> 18:46.470
and just enjoy the festivity.

18:47.930 --> 18:49.810
What are you girls
gonna dress up as?

18:50.750 --> 18:53.580
Witches? Vampires, maybe?

18:59.620 --> 19:01.290
A-ha, here it is.

19:02.400 --> 19:04.830
Mm? Sharon, what is it?
What's happening?

19:08.880 --> 19:09.870
You...

19:42.680 --> 19:43.380
Hey!

19:45.320 --> 19:46.050
Hey!

19:49.090 --> 19:49.920
Listen to me!

19:50.390 --> 19:52.910
Listen, just forget what you just saw.

20:07.510 --> 20:10.440
Why... What is this...
You are...

20:11.840 --> 20:17.150
Linda wasn't feeling well.
She was just sleeping...

20:17.750 --> 20:18.610
Linda...

20:19.720 --> 20:20.550
Linda...

20:41.610 --> 20:44.580
What? What is this?

20:45.610 --> 20:46.600
Linda...

21:30.290 --> 21:32.810
Hey, Mama-san, where's my beer?

21:34.060 --> 21:37.650
Oh, I'm sorry.

21:40.100 --> 21:42.260
Excuse me. I'll be right back.

22:38.050 --> 22:40.960
I don't believe it!
There's actually three of them.

22:42.250 --> 22:43.050
Turn left here.

22:43.940 --> 22:44.930
Aren't they at the base?

22:45.690 --> 22:47.640
- There's the other one.
- Oh, what?

22:48.410 --> 22:50.180
It's all over if we lose this one.
Hurry!

24:24.320 --> 24:25.830
Ted, have you seen Sharon?

24:26.470 --> 24:27.430
No, I haven't.

25:40.330 --> 25:41.050
It's a fake!

26:10.200 --> 26:11.430
What are you doing?

26:11.970 --> 26:12.900
Run for it!

26:29.580 --> 26:31.080
This one is also
heading for the base.

26:31.520 --> 26:34.860
Have the military stand down!
And Louis, look for Saya!

27:06.060 --> 27:09.550
(Laughs) Excuse me, ma'am.
Are you trying to surprise me now?

27:11.110 --> 27:13.000
You're a teacher, ma'am,
what are you doing here?

27:13.540 --> 27:15.620
Shouldn't you be at the party?

27:16.190 --> 27:18.390
Help! A student
changed into a monster!

27:19.470 --> 27:23.470
You're not pulling that one on me,
even if it is Halloween tonight.

27:23.900 --> 27:26.860
No, really!
It just attacked me over there!

27:27.340 --> 27:31.720
Kids these days, they really do
get into these tricks of theirs.

27:31.940 --> 27:34.910
It's not a trick!
Please, believe me! Help me!

27:38.980 --> 27:41.080
Hey, just try to calm down
a little, ma'am.

27:45.170 --> 27:48.470
We used to play little tricks
on teachers we didn't like.

27:48.840 --> 27:51.820
But kids have no reason
to hate a pretty one like yourself.

27:52.080 --> 27:55.320
It's more likely a kid
wanted some attention...

27:56.780 --> 27:58.520
Whoa!

28:37.480 --> 28:38.380
Run!

28:48.500 --> 28:51.740
Hey! Halt! Where are you going?
This area's off-limits!

28:56.730 --> 28:57.730
- Please...
- Stop!

28:58.200 --> 29:00.390
- Help us!
- Who are you, ma'am?

29:01.370 --> 29:02.570
And who is this kid with you?

29:03.730 --> 29:04.450
She's...

29:05.360 --> 29:08.380
Hey, what happened to you?
You're bleeding.

29:10.450 --> 29:11.660
(Nurse) We've just been attacked!

29:12.660 --> 29:15.120
Wait here. I'll call headquarters.

29:16.560 --> 29:17.440
Huh? (Coughs)

29:30.100 --> 29:31.070
Go inside.

29:37.910 --> 29:39.340
What did you just do?

29:40.650 --> 29:43.340
What are you trying to do here?

29:43.850 --> 29:45.180
Shut up!

29:55.830 --> 29:58.920
Listen! Anyone who is
marked by "them" or

29:58.920 --> 30:01.860
anyone who has seen "their" real form,
isn't allowed to live.

30:03.100 --> 30:05.800
So, we've got to kill "them"
before "they" get us.

30:07.940 --> 30:09.410
What are "they"?

30:11.440 --> 30:14.880
Demons. They live off human blood.

30:33.300 --> 30:36.500
Shit! Isn't there something?

30:39.600 --> 30:40.700
Like what?

30:40.700 --> 30:42.000
A weapon.

30:46.780 --> 30:47.640
Here...

30:48.180 --> 30:50.240
That won't kill them.

30:50.850 --> 30:52.210
They won't die

30:52.210 --> 30:55.180
unless they lose enough blood
in one blow.

30:56.220 --> 30:58.280
Then what is this gun for?

30:58.960 --> 31:00.650
You may need it.

31:04.160 --> 31:05.890
You can kill yourself as a last resort.

31:09.790 --> 31:13.360
Dear God help me!
Don't!

31:19.680 --> 31:20.650
Why me?

31:22.480 --> 31:23.810
Who are you?

31:26.450 --> 31:30.750
Why did you help me?

31:31.790 --> 31:36.990
You're lucky. I can't kill "humans."

32:03.060 --> 32:04.080
Shut up!

32:19.840 --> 32:20.860
Wait! Don't shoot!

32:54.120 --> 32:55.220
David!

32:55.580 --> 32:56.340
Saya...

32:58.610 --> 32:59.910
Saya, is that you?!

33:03.780 --> 33:04.970
Open the door!

33:37.800 --> 33:39.160
Fuck! Oh...

33:49.030 --> 33:49.880
Saya!

33:58.670 --> 34:00.260
I can't take this anymore.

34:04.340 --> 34:05.570
Don't give up!

34:05.910 --> 34:07.000
Get the car!

34:07.880 --> 34:09.640
Run the doors down!

34:35.360 --> 34:36.240
Shit!

34:46.920 --> 34:47.610
Saya!

34:52.450 --> 34:53.270
Sword!

35:05.000 --> 35:05.560
(David) You all right?

35:05.560 --> 35:06.610
Saya!

35:28.620 --> 35:29.370
(Saya) Don't!

35:29.710 --> 35:31.670
It's preparing to fly. Take the car.

35:46.270 --> 35:47.490
It's going to take off.

35:54.860 --> 35:55.990
Hurry!

36:00.760 --> 36:01.480
Louis here.

36:02.220 --> 36:03.890
(David) 'The target
is heading for the runway.

36:05.900 --> 36:09.230
'We need to get to the woman
who saw the demon before the cops.'

36:10.170 --> 36:11.040
Roger, you got it.

36:25.850 --> 36:27.170
Shit, it's gonna jump onto it!

36:27.170 --> 36:28.670
Damn it to hell!

36:29.070 --> 36:29.880
(Saya) Just leave it.

36:58.420 --> 37:00.700
- Get closer!
- Don't make it sound so easy!

38:12.160 --> 38:14.070
Saya, where are you going?
You cannot leave!

38:16.600 --> 38:17.350
Saya!

39:53.030 --> 39:54.550
And this is all I know.

39:55.690 --> 39:58.860
I've told you everything
I've seen with my own eyes.

40:00.550 --> 40:02.610
Even though
I'm not sure you believe me.

40:04.580 --> 40:07.800
No, no. We just want to hear
what happened, madam.

40:09.450 --> 40:11.210
I'm not even sure
what really happened.

40:12.780 --> 40:16.560
When I returned to the infirmary,
what should have been Linda's...

40:17.350 --> 40:20.270
I mean, the strange creature's
remains were gone.

40:21.380 --> 40:22.720
No sign of a struggle.

40:23.940 --> 40:25.640
Everything had been wiped clean.

40:27.080 --> 40:28.520
The principal, the teachers,

40:29.390 --> 40:32.810
nobody would believe me
when I told them what had happened.

40:36.440 --> 40:40.240
I know, the man that was with her,
she called him David.

40:40.940 --> 40:42.860
Doesn't he work in this building?

40:43.640 --> 40:46.570
He would know what happened.
Where is he?

40:50.470 --> 40:53.080
Madam,
no one fitting your description

40:53.680 --> 40:55.370
works or is stationed at this base.

40:55.820 --> 40:58.550
- That can't be, he...
- I'm sorry, madam,

40:58.920 --> 41:00.760
we don't have
any further information.

41:07.920 --> 41:13.090
Before you go, the girl you saw...
did she look like this?

42:49.170 --> 42:54.570
After all,
I never understood what I saw.

42:55.670 --> 43:01.170
That girl Saya and the creatures
she killed all remained a mystery.

43:01.780 --> 43:05.480
Only two students were noted
as having left for other schools.

43:07.250 --> 43:11.210
Could she still be somewhere
around the base?

43:12.460 --> 43:15.760
Is she still fighting those creatures?

43:16.430 --> 43:20.490
Just as we humans continue
to kill each other.

43:22.170 --> 43:25.830
That beautiful,
yet dangerous living thing

43:29.710 --> 43:32.510
(Radio) 'The liberation front has
attacked the American Blake base.

43:33.070 --> 43:36.200
'In retaliation,
B-52s from Yokota base in Japan

43:36.460 --> 43:39.370
'have been ordered
to fly to North Vietnam.'

43:59.280 --> 44:09.080
Readjusted By Sooraj
